# nr-tui-term-input: wire lines for the new crate mixdog-term (native/core/crates/mixdog-term)

The crate is written but not compiled inside the workspace (it is not a member yet). Its input module was compiled and tested
outside the workspace with rustc only (59 unit tests, the 3801-entry Ink twin in tests/keys_twin.rs, clippy -D warnings); the
rest of the crate (Cargo features of windows-sys / windows / signal-hook, the dev-dependencies) has not been compiled.

## native/core/Cargo.toml

1. [workspace] members: after `"crates/mixdog-connections",` and before `"crates/mixdog-cli",` add
       "crates/mixdog-term",
2. [workspace.dependencies], internal crates, after the `mixdog-connections = { path = "crates/mixdog-connections" }` line add
       mixdog-term = { path = "crates/mixdog-term" }
3. [workspace.dependencies], alphabetical among the others, add (all four are in the local cargo cache; `windows` 0.62.2 is
   already in Cargo.lock, the other three are not and need new lock entries with their dependencies):
       portable-pty = "0.9.0"
       signal-hook = "0.3.18"
       vte = "0.14.1"
       windows = { version = "0.62.2", default-features = false }

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Add the packages of portable-pty 0.9.0 (nix 0.28, filedescriptor 0.8.3, serial2 0.2, shared_library 0.1.9, winreg 0.10.1,
winapi 0.3.9, downcast-rs, shell-words), signal-hook 0.3.18 (signal-hook-registry 1.4.8 is already locked), vte 0.14.1, and the
`mixdog-term` package. The crate's third-party dependencies are, per the manifest: base64, serde, serde_json, tempfile (dev),
libc and signal-hook (unix), windows-sys and windows (windows), vte and portable-pty (dev).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Re-run the workspace-hack generator if the build gate checks it: mixdog-term's manifest does not carry the
`mixdog-workspace-hack` line (mixdog-js, mixdog-patch and the other native-tool crates do not either).

## compose_flip.rs / protocol tables

Nothing: this crate registers no service and no protocol method.
